D. Spliced proof interface
  m=1: HYP-3431 supplies the canonical rank-6 corridor-fence base;
       HYP-3457 gives the exact finite survivor windows.
  m=2..4: HYP-3437/HYP-3439 rank drops to the rank-5 core
          (5,7,9,11,13), and HYP-3457 supplies the finite windows.
  m>=5: the checked rank-5 overlap descent is stable through m=70;
        HYP-3454 gives the rank-one endpoint interval and HYP-3456
        gives the mod-35 boundary count.
  This removes the AP84 splice as an unnamed HYP-3439 obligation.  The
  remaining global proof work is the non-AP primitive-row transfer through
  HYP-3453/HYP-3451/HYP-3455 or named owner/current/state-lift debt.

